> This is the uncompressed size, it should be documented. Could we set it to -1 if we actually hit the body_size_limit?
> 
> Now that I remembered we have the body_size_limit parameter, I think the name scrape_body_size_bytes would be more appropriate. Thanks!

I added a new `bodySizeLimit` field into `scrapeLoop` struct, which set by `int64(sp.config.BodySizeLimit)` at `newScrapeLoop()`. Finally, I use the following logic, I guess this is what you are looking for?

```golang
if int64(len(b)) > sl.bodySizeLimit {
	bytes = -1
} else {
	bytes = len(b)
}
```
